# dark-gray - literal colours to rewrite inside the upstream GTK stylesheet.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# palette.css redefines GTK's named colours, which works only for themes that
# actually USE those names. Juno-ocean-v40 does not: it was compiled from SASS
# with the accent inlined, so gtk-3.0/gtk-dark.css contains #00A9A5 as a
# literal 112 times and mentions @theme_selected_bg_color exactly once - on its
# own @define-color line, which nothing then reads. Redefining the name is
# therefore inert, and the desktop stays teal no matter what palette.css says.
#
# set-theme.sh fixes that by generating a recoloured COPY of the upstream
# stylesheet into ~/.cache/themes/ and importing that instead of the original.
# ~/.themes is never modified.
#
# FORMAT
#
#   <source-hex>  <palette-colour-name>
#
# Matching is case-insensitive and covers both spellings the SASS emits:
#   #00A9A5                    -> the palette colour
#   rgba(0, 169, 165, 0.6)     -> the palette colour at that same alpha
#
# The right-hand side must be an @define-color name defined in palette.css.
# An unknown name is reported and skipped rather than silently ignored.

# Primary accent - selection, focus rings, active tabs, checked switches.
#
# Target theme_selected_bg_color, NOT accent_bg_color. palette.css defines both
# (accent_bg_color is libadwaita's spelling of the same colour), and derive.py
# resolves the Qt side as theme_selected_bg_color first - so aiming the two at
# different names meant editing one moved GTK while editing the other moved
# Dolphin. Same colour, one name, everywhere.
00A9A5  theme_selected_bg_color
# Its darker companion, used for pressed states and accent borders.
007673  accent_dark_color

# Secondary accent. Juno uses this orange for checkboxes, radios and progress.
# Assets carry it too, so it is recoloured in the PNGs as well.
F78C6C  theme_selected_bg_color

# Status colours, so error/warning surfaces match palette.css.
FF2046  error_color
FF3A5B  error_color
FF5370  error_color
56CEFF  success_color

# ── Asset colours ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The PNGs in the theme's assets/ dir were generated from a DIFFERENT palette
# than the stylesheet - measured, not one of the hexes above appears in them.
# So they need their own entries, or checkboxes and window buttons keep the old
# colours while everything around them changes.
#
# Matching for assets is nearest-colour within a small radius, so the
# antialiased variants (#d08771, #d0876f, ...) follow their base colour.
#
# Where each one is used, measured across the 230 PNGs:
D08770  theme_selected_bg_color   # checkbox / radio / switch fill  (52 files)
13A0BF  theme_selected_bg_color   # grid + menu selection, scale slider (6 files)
37B9A5  theme_selected_bg_color   # calendar-selected (1 file)
EBCB8B  warning_color     # titlebar minimise button (3 files)
BF616A  error_color       # titlebar close button (2 files)
A3BE8C  success_color     # titlebar maximise button (2 files)

# ── The rest of Juno's palette ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The accent is not the only thing this theme baked in - it inlined EVERY
# colour. Counted in gtk-3.0/gtk-dark.css: #BFC3C4 (its foreground) 124 times,
# #040407 (its borders) 113, #131520 (its base) 49, #0F111A (its window bg) 41.
#
# So @theme_bg_color and friends were just as inert as @theme_selected_bg_color
# was. A palette.css edit changed the NAME lookup - which is all the ags bar
# reads, and why the bar tracked the palette while apps did not - but every
# actual painted surface in a GTK app still came from these literals.
#
# Mapping them is what finally makes palette.css authoritative for GTK.

# Surfaces, darkest first. Kept as distinct shades rather than collapsed onto
# one colour, so the theme keeps its sense of depth.
090B10  surface_sunken_color   # sunken frames, scrollbar troughs
0A0B11  surface_sunken_color
0D0F17  sidebar_bg_color       # sidebars, gutters
0F111A  theme_bg_color         # window background
131520  theme_base_color       # entries, lists, text views
151722  insensitive_bg_color   # disabled surfaces
151724  theme_unfocused_base_color
191C2C  button_bg_color        # button face
1A1E2D  button_hover_bg_color
31363D  button_active_bg_color

# Borders.
040407  borders
050509  unfocused_borders

# Foregrounds.
BFC3C4  theme_fg_color
D1D1D1  theme_fg_color
CCCFD0  theme_fg_color
FEFEFE  theme_selected_fg_color   # text on an accent fill
9DA1A4  insensitive_fg_color
676A6F  insensitive_fg_color
646669  insensitive_fg_color
